---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
import { coreExperienceCards } from '../data/site';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Experiences',href:'/experiences/'}];
const additional=[
  {title:'Wildlife & Nature',image:images.wildlife,copy:'Nature-led journeys where landscapes, wildlife, and local environments are central to the itinerary.',href:'/custom-group-trip-planning/'},
  {title:'Water & Island Travel',image:images.water,copy:'Diving, snorkeling, sailing, paddling, island travel, and coastal itineraries for groups that want more time in and around the water.',href:'/group-travel/dive-communities/'},
  {title:'Wellness & Active Rest',image:images.lake,copy:'Trips that combine movement, recovery, culture, nature, and time together without turning every day into a performance objective.',href:'/group-travel/wellness-yoga/'},
  {title:'Social & Affinity Travel',image:images.heroAlt,copy:'Private journeys for communities, alumni, women’s groups, friend groups, and organizers whose shared connection is the main reason to travel.',href:'/group-travel/social-affinity/'},
  {title:'Business & Team Travel',image:images.city,copy:'Experience-led company and team travel that can combine shared activity, culture, downtime, and selected work sessions.',href:'/group-travel/businesses-teams/'},
  {title:'Selected Public Departures',image:images.coast,copy:'Hosted or joinable trips released when real dates, pricing, suppliers, and participation requirements are ready to publish.',href:'/join-a-trip/'}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Group Travel Experiences | Talon Expeditions" description="Explore Talon Expeditions travel styles including private group travel, learn-to trips, trekking and active travel, cultural and cruise travel, wildlife, wellness, water, and hosted group journeys." image={images.coast} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="hub-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.coast}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Talon Expeditions experiences</p><h1 class="section-title">Choose the reason to go. We can help build the travel around it.</h1><p class="lead">Talon Expeditions is not limited to one definition of adventure. A trip can be physically demanding, skill-based, cultural, social, comfort-forward, water-focused, wildlife-led, or a blend of several styles. The common thread is a more intentional journey with enough support to make the group work.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">How to use this page</p><h2>Start with the travel style that sounds closest to your group.</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>What kinds of trips does Talon Expeditions plan?</h2><p>Talon Expeditions plans private and supported group travel including trekking, hiking, learn-to trips, diving, skiing, mountaineering, wilderness skills, cultural travel, cruises, wildlife and nature trips, wellness travel, business-team travel, and other experience-led itineraries. Specific trips can combine several styles when the group and destination support it.</p></div><p>The categories below are planning paths, not rigid product boxes. A hiking club may want a cultural extension. A cruise group may want active shore days. A learn-to dive trip may include non-divers. A company team may prefer a light active itinerary rather than a conventional corporate retreat.</p><p>Use the categories to understand what each format changes about the itinerary, support, readiness, and group structure. Then use the planning form when the real trip falls between them.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Core travel paths</p><h2 class="section-title">The main ways we structure group travel.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">These pages carry the deepest commercial and planning detail because they represent the strongest long-term Talon Expeditions offers.</p></div><div class="destination-grid">{coreExperienceCards.map((item)=><a class="destination-card" href={item.href} style={`background-image:url('${item.image}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">{item.eyebrow}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.copy}</p><div class="mini-tags"><span>Planning</span><span>Support</span><span>Worldwide</span></div></div></a>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">More ways to travel</p><h2 class="section-title">Build the experience around the community.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">The supporting categories let us be broad without turning the site into a generic “we do everything” travel agency.</p></div><div class="destination-grid">{additional.map((item)=><a class="destination-card" href={item.href} style={`background-image:url('${item.image}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">Experience-led travel</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.copy}</p></div></a>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section tabbed-feature"><div class="shell tabbed-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">How to choose</p><h2 class="section-title">Start with what should be protected when tradeoffs appear.</h2><ul class="category-menu"><li class="active">The activity</li><li>The people</li><li>The destination</li><li>The learning goal</li><li>The social experience</li><li>The comfort level</li></ul></div><div class="category-feature" style={`background-image:url('${images.trekking}')`}><div class="feature-note"><h3>Every trip eventually makes tradeoffs.</h3><p>More activity can mean less cultural time. More destinations can mean more transfers. More privacy can cost more. More flexibility can require more transport or staffing. The group should decide what matters most before those tradeoffs become expensive.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Not sure where it fits?</p><h2 class="section-title">A good trip does not need to match a website category perfectly.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">The site architecture exists to make the options understandable and searchable. The actual itinerary can cross categories when that creates a better journey.</p></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="/custom-group-trip-planning/"><small>Custom planning</small><strong>Build a trip around your own combination</strong></a><a class="related-card" href="/group-travel/"><small>Organizer path</small><strong>Start with the type of group</strong></a><a class="related-card" href="/resources/"><small>Planning library</small><strong>Start with a question or problem</strong></a></div></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="The best category is the one that gets us close enough to start the real conversation." />
</BaseLayout>
